/// \class CallHelpOnDamage
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_die_damage_collide_module_factories
/// \brief Damage module registered as "CallHelpOnDamage": when its object
///        is hurt, nearby units are called to help.
///
/// Read from the matched BFME 2 body: on damage of a type in
/// \c DamageTypes, and at most once per \c CallDelay, the module searches
/// the partition manager for objects within \c CallRadius of its object
/// that pass a filter chain built from the controlling player and the
/// \c ValidObjects filter. Each one with an AI is given an AI command
/// aimed at the attacker when \c MoveToAttacker is set and the attacker
/// still exists, and at the damaged object otherwise. Which command that
/// is, is not identified here. The frame of the next allowed call is the
/// module's saved state.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Own fields (CallHelpOnDamageModuleData): \c DamageTypes (damage type
/// flags, default all), \c CallRadius (real, default 100), \c CallDelay
/// (milliseconds, stored as logic frames), \c MoveToAttacker (boolean,
/// default false) and \c ValidObjects (an object filter). The parse
/// procedure adds an empty table before the class's own table, so these
/// are the only fields.
///
/// \par Remastering
/// The constructor default for \c CallDelay is four times the logic frame
/// rate global, four seconds' worth of logic frames, and is not converted
/// like a parsed value.
///
/// \see CallHelpOnDamage::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      CallHelpOnDamageModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class CallHelpOnDamageModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_die_damage_collide_module_factories
