/// \class HordeTransportContainDamage
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_die_damage_collide_module_factories
/// \brief Damage module registered as "HordeTransportContainDamage": a
///        transport that carries hordes loses horde members as it loses
///        health.
///
/// Read from the matched BFME 2 body of its damage callback (the entry its
/// damage interface calls): as the transport loses health, the
/// module kills members of the hordes it carries, so that each horde's
/// size follows the transport's health in steps, scaled to the horde's
/// member limit. Which contained objects count as hordes, and their
/// member counts and limits, come from accessors identified only by their
/// place in virtual tables (and, for the horde test, an unnamed template
/// flag), so this reading is an inference.
///
/// \par Modding
/// The module has no fields: its data factory allocates only the base
/// module data, and its parse procedure adds an empty table. Which
/// objects carry it, and the horde member limits of what they carry, are
/// the data that matter.
///
/// \see HordeTransportContainDamage::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      HordeTransportContainDamageModuleData::friend_newModuleData

