/// \class ReflectDamage
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_die_damage_collide_module_factories
/// \brief Damage module registered as "ReflectDamage": part of the damage
///        its object takes is dealt back to the attacker.
///
/// Read from the matched BFME 2 body: on damage of a type in
/// \c DamageTypesToReflect, when the attacker still exists, the module
/// builds a new damage event from its own object and applies it to the
/// attacker through Object::attemptDamage. The amount is the incoming
/// damage times \c ReflectDamagePercentage, but never less than
/// \c MinimumDamageToReflect. The reflected damage carries a special
/// damage type that ReflectDamage itself ignores, so two reflecting
/// objects do not bounce damage back and forth.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Own fields (ReflectDamageModuleData): \c DamageTypesToReflect (damage
/// type flags), \c ReflectDamagePercentage (a percentage) and
/// \c MinimumDamageToReflect (real). All three default to zero, so a block
/// without \c DamageTypesToReflect reflects nothing. Because the minimum
/// is a floor, a non-zero \c MinimumDamageToReflect returns at least that
/// much for every matching hit, however small.
///
/// \see ReflectDamage::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      ReflectDamageModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class ReflectDamageModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_die_damage_collide_module_factories
/// \brief Module data for ReflectDamage: the damage types, share and
///        minimum to reflect.
///
