/// \class EvacuateDamage
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_die_damage_collide_module_factories
/// \brief Damage module registered as "EvacuateDamage": reacts to hits
///        from the weapon its data names, with exit orders among others,
///        and to damage of one type totalled over a short time span.
///
/// Read from the matched BFME 2 bodies. The module's damage entry (the
/// first slot of its damage interface) first looks up the attacker; if the
/// attacker no longer exists or has no current weapon, the hit is ignored.
/// - **Named weapon.** When the name of the attacker's current weapon
///   template equals \c WeaponThatCausesEvacuation, the module turns to an
///   interface on its own object that this page does not identify, and
///   returns after it. Depending on a test on that interface, it either
///   makes a single call on it, or walks the entries it lists and issues
///   each entry an AI command naming the module's own object:
///   AICommandInterface::aiExit, or, for entries with a particular state
///   flag set, another AI command that this page does not identify.
/// - **Tracked damage type.** Only when the weapon does not match, and the
///   damage is of the type named by \c DamageTypeToTrack, does the module
///   go on to its tracking step. If the object has a body, that step
///   records the amount and the logic frame, then adds up the
///   records younger than \c TrackingTimeSpan, dropping older ones. When
///   that sum reaches the object's current health times
///   \c DamageToPanicThreshold and the attacker still exists, it turns to
///   another part of the object that this page does not identify. If the
///   object has that part, the module clears its records and issues an AI
///   command concerning the attacker through it.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Own fields (EvacuateDamageModuleData): \c WeaponThatCausesEvacuation
/// (a weapon name), \c DamageTypeToTrack (one damage type name, default
/// \c PIERCE), \c DamageToPanicThreshold (a percentage, default 10%) and
/// \c TrackingTimeSpan (milliseconds, stored as logic frames).
///
/// \par Remastering
/// The constructor default for \c TrackingTimeSpan is a fixed count of
/// logic frames, so its real-time length depends on the logic rate.
///
/// \see EvacuateDamage::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      EvacuateDamageModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class EvacuateDamageModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_die_damage_collide_module_factories
/// \brief Module data for EvacuateDamage: the tracked damage type, the
///        threshold, the time span and a weapon name.
///
/// Built once per module line by EvacuateDamageModuleData::friend_newModuleData
/// and shared by every object of the template. The class's identity rests
/// on the ModuleFactory registration and on the parse procedure its
/// factory passes.

