/// \class AODCrushCollide
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_die_damage_collide_module_factories
/// \brief Collide and update module registered as "AODCrushCollide": an
///        object that damages non-allied objects it runs into, with effects
///        chosen by the victim's size.
///
/// Read from the matched BFME 2 bodies:
/// - **Contact.** The collide step first skips contacts that state checks
///   on either object rule out and ignores allies of its object. Next, if
///   its object is contained, it asks the contain module of the containing
///   object for the record that HordeMemberCollide also reads there (the
///   same contain-interface slot, identified only by its place in the
///   virtual table) and, when there is one, makes a call on that record
///   with its own object and the other object; what the call does is not
///   identified here. An object that is not contained makes no such call.
///   Only after that does it apply further checks on the other object (a
///   status bit and its body), so a contact those checks reject may
///   already have reached the record. For a contact that passes them, it
///   runs the timer step below and then damages the other object with its
///   object as the source: with \c SpecialDamage, \c SpecialDamageType
///   and \c SpecialDeathType when the other object passes the
///   \c SpecialObject filter, and with \c Damage, \c DamageType and
///   \c DeathType otherwise. In the special case its own object also takes
///   \c SelfDamage of \c SelfDamageType and \c SelfDeathType, with the
///   other object as the source. Finally it plays the FX list and runs the
///   object creation list for the other object's size: small, medium or
///   large, read from a size category on the other object's template.
/// - **Timer.** A contact that passes the checks starts the timer when it
///   is not running, setting a state bit on its own object (the
///   reconstruction reads it as a model condition) and waking the update
///   step; every such contact moves the expiry frame two seconds ahead.
///   The update step clears the bit once that frame has passed and then
///   sleeps until the next contact.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Own fields (AODCrushCollideModuleData): \c SmallFXList,
/// \c SmallObjectCreationList, \c MediumFXList, \c MediumObjectCreationList,
/// \c LargeFXList and \c LargeObjectCreationList; \c Damage, \c DamageType
/// and \c DeathType; \c SpecialObject (an object filter) with
/// \c SpecialDamage, \c SpecialDamageType and \c SpecialDeathType; and
/// \c SelfDamage, \c SelfDamageType and \c SelfDeathType. The damage types
/// default to \c CRUSH, the death types to \c NORMAL and the amounts to
/// zero. Which template field holds the size category is not identified
/// here. Because the module damages objects, it is game logic and must
/// behave identically on every machine.
///
/// \par Remastering
/// The two-second window is twice the global logic frame rate, computed at
/// run time rather than read from INI.
///
/// \see AODCrushCollide::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      AODCrushCollideModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class AODCrushCollideModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_die_damage_collide_module_factories
/// \brief Module data for AODCrushCollide: per-size FX and creation lists,
///        and the normal, special and self damage settings.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// AODCrushCollideModuleData::friend_newModuleData and shared by every
/// object of the template.

/// \fn Module *AODCrushCollide::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "AODCrushCollide": creates the
///        module for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration when an
/// object whose template lists the module is built. The module it builds
/// is both a collide module and an update module, as the registration's
/// interface mask says (group page).
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's module data for this module line,
///                    shared with every other object of the template.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see AODCrushCollide

/// \fn ModuleData *AODCrushCollideModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "AODCrushCollide": creates the module
///        data for one module line and parses its block.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through the registration
/// while object INI loads. The constructor clears the six list fields,
/// sets the defaults listed on the AODCrushCollide page and constructs the
/// \c SpecialObject filter. When \p ini is not null, the factory passes
