/// \class CrateCollide
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_die_damage_collide_module_factories
/// \brief Base of the crate collide modules: an object that something can
///        pick up by touching it.
///
/// Read from the matched BFME 2 bodies: on contact, the module asks
/// CrateCollide::isValidToExecute whether the toucher may pick the crate
/// up. That check applies the pickup rules from the data (among them
/// \c RequiredKindOf and \c ForbiddenKindOf, \c ForbidOwnerPlayer,
/// \c BuildingPickup, \c HumanOnly and \c PickupScience) and refuses
/// neutral or dead touchers and a crate that has already been used. If the
/// pickup is valid, the derived class's crate behavior runs; when that
/// succeeds, \c ExecuteFX plays on the toucher, the crate marks itself as
/// used and is destroyed. Whenever the pickup is valid, whether or not the
/// crate behavior succeeds, the animation named by \c ExecuteAnimation (if
/// it is set and the game shows such icons) is added to the world at the
/// crate's position, using \c ExecuteAnimationTime and
/// \c ExecuteAnimationZRise.
/// Zero Hour has the same field table. Its CrateCollide has no used flag,
/// which BFME 2 adds to the pickup check and to the module's saved state,
/// and some of its other pickup checks differ.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Fields (CrateCollideModuleData): \c RequiredKindOf, \c ForbiddenKindOf,
/// \c ForbidOwnerPlayer, \c BuildingPickup, \c HumanOnly, \c PickupScience,
/// \c ExecuteFX, \c ExecuteAnimation, \c ExecuteAnimationTime,
/// \c ExecuteAnimationZRise and \c ExecuteAnimationFades, the same eleven
/// as Zero Hour's table. No module is registered under the name
/// \c CrateCollide. The registration table pairs
/// CrateCollideModuleData::friend_newModuleData with \c HealCrateCollide
/// and \c ShroudCrateCollide, so blocks for those two accept exactly these
/// fields; the other crate collides have data factories of their own.
///
/// \see CrateCollideModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class CrateCollideModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_die_damage_collide_module_factories
/// \brief Module data of the crate collides: who may pick a crate up and
///        what plays when it is used.
///
/// Built once per module line by CrateCollideModuleData::friend_newModuleData
/// for the \c HealCrateCollide and \c ShroudCrateCollide names, and shared
/// by every object of the template.

/// \fn ModuleData *CrateCollideModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory that the registration table pairs with
///        "HealCrateCollide" and "ShroudCrateCollide": creates the crate
///        data for one module line and parses its block.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through either
/// registration while object INI loads; no registration names it under
/// \c CrateCollide. When \p ini is not null, the factory passes
/// CrateCollideModuleData::buildFieldParse to INI::initFromINIMultiProc.
///
/// \param ini  The INI reader positioned at the module's block. When null,
///             parsing is skipped and the data keeps its defaults.
/// \return The new module data as the ModuleData base the factory stores,
///         or null when the allocation fails.
/// \see CrateCollide


/// \class HordeMemberCollide
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_die_damage_collide_module_factories
/// \brief Collide module registered as "HordeMemberCollide": lets a horde
///        member's contacts reach the horde that contains it.
///
/// Read from the matched BFME 2 body. The horde record below, and the
/// methods called on it, are identified only by their place in virtual
/// tables. The collide step does nothing unless its object is contained
/// by an object whose contain module has a horde record that names an
/// object (the tracked object). A contact with the tracked object is
/// handed to the record. Otherwise, after a check on the record that can
/// end the step, a contact with an object inside the tracked object is
/// handed over too. For any other contact, when the toucher (or its
/// container) has a particular kind-of bit, is allied and has a horde
/// record of its own that passes two further checks (one of them given
/// the tracked object), the module hands the record its own tracked object
/// rather than the toucher. What the record does with what it is handed
/// is not identified here.
///
/// \par Modding
/// HordeMemberCollide accepts no fields: the registration pairs it with
/// the data factory that is also registered under \c SquishCollide, which
/// allocates only the base module data and whose parse procedure adds
/// nothing.
///
/// \see HordeMemberCollide::friend_newModuleInstance

/// \fn Module *HordeMemberCollide::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "HordeMemberCollide": creates the
///        module for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration when an
/// object whose template lists the module is built. The module data it
/// receives comes from the data factory registered for both
/// \c HordeMemberCollide and \c SquishCollide.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's module data for this module line,
///                    shared with every other object of the template.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see HordeMemberCollide
